  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively establish related ingredients: controlled high-temperature or in situ vacuum heating of HEAs (especially R7 and R9), temperature-dependent behavior in HEA nanosystems (R15 and R16), surface-free-energy effects (R5), irradiation- or processing-induced elemental redistribution (R8, R10, R12, and R13), and selective compositional loss during energetic processing (R14). R7 also reports preferential depletion of one constituent during vacuum/air heating, while R10 reports segregation in a nanostructured refractory HEA. However, none describes AuCoCuNiPt nanoparticles, heating-driven Au/Cu surface segregation, non-sluggish diffusion promoted by particle reshaping, or subsequent selective melting/evaporation. Thus the literature points generally toward thermally activated redistribution and surface-sensitive composition changes, but connecting these ideas to surface-energy-driven Au/Cu segregation and evaporation in sub-10-nm HENA particles would require a substantial new idea."
